    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a high-upside core anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (76.64) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92). **Corbin Carroll** remains our premier offensive engine against Phillips, benefiting from an elite lineup spot and favorable platoon dynamics. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** secures our top spot due to a massive +14% platoon edge and a projected wind advantage that pushes his efficiency rating into the \"Strong\" tier. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention with a 70.84 score; facing the vulnerable Ryan Feltner, his capacity to capitalize on the pitcher\u2019s 4.55 xERA makes him a cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive strategy. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our top-tier plays (69.19), as the hitter-friendly park environment more than offsets the challenge posed by Kyle Bradish.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket was the exclusion of **Austin Riley** (54.04). Despite a solid individual projection, he narrowly missed the cut behind the superior platoon advantages and order-driven scoring of **Gabriel Moreno** (60.52) and **Kyle Karros** (55.84). We are monitoring significant volatility for our fringe starters; **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all face a notable 30\u201338% rain risk. Furthermore, while **Cole Young** (50.51) occupies a premium lead-off spot, his matchup against Kyle Bradish is tempered by the pitcher\u2019s ability to suppress stolen base opportunities, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining lineup to chase our SB goals. Owners should keep a close eye on final lineup confirmations for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, and **Kyle Karros**, as any shift in batting order will require immediate recalibration of their efficiency scores.",
